# src/syncai_lio_bridge, from SyncAI-LIO-Bridge: the LIO -> planar odom / TF
# bridge, the stack's only odometry source. Managed with vcstool, the same way
# robot-state.repos manages src/syncai_robot_state, driver-manager.repos manages
# src/syncai_driver_manager, interface.repos manages src/syncai_common and
# third-party.repos manages src/third-party/.
#
#   vcs import < lio-bridge.repos          # populate a fresh clone
#   vcs import < lio-bridge.repos --force  # re-checkout after changing the pin
#
# The key already carries `src/`, so run this from the workspace root without an
# extra `src` argument, or the package lands in `src/src/`.
#
# It left this repository in 2026-10, the third package that month to go out to
# its own repo and be rewritten against rclrs (Rust) -- after
# driver-manager.repos and robot-state.repos. The ROS surface is deliberately
# identical: same package name, same `lio_bridge_node` node and executable, same
# `lio_bridge.launch.py` (byte-for-byte the rclcpp one -- it still reads
# [system] robot_id from the INI and passes every parameter inline; there is no
# params file, so the bare-`/**` key the other two Rust packages needed does not
# arise here), same topics, frames, message types and QoS. So
# config/sessions/start_nav.yaml did not move. What changed is inside the
# package, and its README lists every deviation; the ones worth knowing from
# here:
#
#   - TF is the node's own, not tf2_ros (rclrs has no binding): a /tf +
#     /tf_static subscription keeping only the newest transform per child frame,
#     and a plain /tf publisher with TransformBroadcaster's QoS. The C++ looked
#     up at TimePointZero, so nothing it relied on is lost -- including the
#     shared quirk that a localizer which dies after relocalizing leaves its last
#     map -> pointlio_odom bridged forever.
#   - A malformed pointlio/lio_odom pose (NaN, non-unit quaternion) is dropped
#     with a throttled warning instead of being broadcast as a NaN transform.
#   - Parameters are read-only and `publish_rate` / `transform_tolerance` are
#     validated (a non-positive rate falls back to 1 Hz, a negative tolerance to
#     0) -- the C++ silently accepted both.
#   - No SIGINT handler: rclrs handles no signals, so shutdown is the default
#     action and Drop does not run.
#
# `src/syncai_lio_bridge/` is gitignored -- edit the node in that checkout (its
# own git repo) and commit there, never here; the next --force import overwrites
# anything uncommitted.
#
# Tracks `dev`, that repo's working branch, like the other three first-party
# .repos files. (Its `main` still holds only the initial commit.)
#
# HTTPS rather than the SSH remote: the repo is public, so the build container
# needs no keys. `git@github.com:chungweeeei/SyncAI-LIO-Bridge.git` is the same
# checkout for anyone who prefers to push over SSH.
#
# Like the other two, this is an `ament_cargo` package whose Rust message crates
# (std_msgs / geometry_msgs / nav_msgs / sensor_msgs) come from the image's
# ros2-rust underlay (/opt/ros2_rust_underlay) -- see driver-manager.repos and
# the Dockerfile's underlay stanza. And like syncai_robot_state, its `tf2_msgs`
# is the exception: the ros-humble-tf2-msgs deb already ships generated Rust
# bindings, so it needs nothing from the underlay.
repositories:
  src/syncai_lio_bridge:
    type: git
    url: https://github.com/chungweeeei/SyncAI-LIO-Bridge.git
    version: dev
